{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# SAM 3 & Open-Vocabulary Segmentation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Prompt construction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build a helper that turns a user sentence into a list of SAM 3 concept prompts. This is the boundary where \"what the user typed\" meets \"what the model consumes\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def split_concepts(sentence):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Heuristic splitter for multi-concept prompts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Returns list of short noun phrases."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sep in [\",\", \";\", \"and\", \"or\", \"&\"]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if sep in sentence:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            parts = [p.strip() for p in sentence.replace(\"and \", \",\").split(\",\")]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return [p for p in parts if p]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [sentence.strip()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(split_concepts(\"cats, dogs and balloons\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "SAM 3 accepts one concept per forward pass; for multi-concept queries, loop or batch them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Post-processing helpers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Turn SAM 3's raw outputs into a clean list of detections that match our Phase 4 Lesson 16 pipeline contract."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from dataclasses import dataclass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from typing import List"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@dataclass"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ConceptDetection:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    concept: str"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    instance_id: int"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    box: tuple          # (x1, y1, x2, y2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score: float"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask_rle: str       # run-length encoded"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rle_encode(binary_mask):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    flat = binary_mask.flatten().astype(\"uint8\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    runs = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prev, count = flat[0], 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for v in flat:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if v == prev:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            count += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            runs.append((int(prev), count))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            prev, count = v, 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    runs.append((int(prev), count))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return \";\".join(f\"{v}x{c}\" for v, c in runs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "RLE keeps response payloads small even for many high-resolution masks. The same format works across SAM 2, SAM 3, Grounded SAM 2."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: A unified open-vocab segmentation interface"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wrap whatever backend you have (SAM 3, Grounded SAM 2, YOLO-World + SAM 2) behind a single method. Your downstream code does not change when the backend does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from abc import ABC, abstractmethod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class OpenVocabSeg(ABC):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    @abstractmethod"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def detect(self, image: np.ndarray, concept: str) -> List[ConceptDetection]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ..."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class StubOpenVocabSeg(OpenVocabSeg):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Deterministic stub used for pipeline testing when real models are not loaded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def detect(self, image, concept):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, w = image.shape[:2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ConceptDetection("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                concept=concept,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                instance_id=0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                box=(w * 0.2, h * 0.3, w * 0.5, h * 0.8),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score=0.89,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mask_rle=\"0x100;1x50;0x200\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ConceptDetection("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                concept=concept,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                instance_id=1,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                box=(w * 0.55, h * 0.25, w * 0.85, h * 0.75),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                score=0.74,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mask_rle=\"0x80;1x40;0x220\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The real `SAM3OpenVocabSeg` subclass would wrap `transformers.Sam3Model` and `Sam3Processor`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Hugging Face SAM 3 usage (reference)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For the actual model, the `transformers` integration:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import Sam3Processor, Sam3Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "processor = Sam3Processor.from_pretrained(\"facebook/sam3\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = Sam3Model.from_pretrained(\"facebook/sam3\").eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "inputs = processor(images=pil_image, return_tensors=\"pt\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "inputs = processor.set_text_prompt(inputs, \"yellow school bus\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outputs = model(**inputs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "masks = processor.post_process_masks("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    outputs.masks, inputs.original_sizes, inputs.reshaped_input_sizes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "boxes = outputs.boxes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scores = outputs.scores"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One prompt, all matches returned in a single call."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Measure what Grounded SAM 2 gave you for free"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "An honest benchmark: what happens when you replace Grounded SAM 2 with SAM 3 in a real pipeline?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Latency: SAM 3 saves one forward pass (no separate detector) but the model itself is heavier; usually net-neutral or a slight speedup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Accuracy: SAM 3 substantially better on rare or compositional concepts (\"striped red umbrella\"). Similar on common single-word concepts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Flexibility: Grounded SAM 2 lets you swap detectors (DINO-X, Florence-2, Grounding DINO 1.5); SAM 3 is monolithic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Conclusion: SAM 3 is the default for 2026 open-vocab seg. Grounded SAM 2 is still the right answer when you need detector flexibility or different license terms."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Run SAM 3 on 10 images with concept prompts you choose. Compare against SAM 2 + Grounding DINO 1.5 on the same images. Report which concepts each model missed.\n2. **(Medium)** Build a \"click-to-include / click-to-exclude\" UI on top of SAM 3: a text prompt returns candidate instances; user clicks keep which ones count as positive. Output the final concept set as JSON.\n3. **(Hard)** Fine-tune SAM 3 on a custom concept set (e.g. 5 types of electronic components) with 20 labelled images each. Compare to zero-shot SAM 3 on the same test set; measure mask IoU improvement."
      ]
    }
